{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1258573-binding-your-own-paperbacks-and-hardbacks","id":1258573,"title":"Binding your Own Paperbacks and Hardbacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-02T11:56:43-07:00","id":1258573,"title":"Binding your Own Paperbacks and Hardbacks","content":"I've purchased a little over 100 DrivethruRPG PDFs and I'm going to start binding some into paperbacks and some into hardbacks. Has anyone bound their own paperbacks? If so, what did you do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T13:01:21-07:00","id":1258582,"title":"","content":"I've sewn-bound (Smyth style) my own books, but nothing longer than ~40 pages, and used a press to do spiral and comb-binding.<br /> <br /> It's... a lot of work and gets expensive if you plan on doing a lot of it. Unless you're really into doing your own binding (which I can understand for RPGs, the standard bindings DTRPG uses are a good compromise of price and quality, but I could see wanting to go cheaper for books you're going to wear out, or more expensive bindings for ones you want to hold up to a lot), is there a reason not to just PoD the books you purchased?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T14:08:37-07:00","id":1258589,"title":"","content":"The average supplement (ignoring core books, fat splats, and such) comes out to about 100 pages which for 20 lb paper is going to be 0.35&quot;. From what I could find, this seemed comfortably within the limits of what one could do at home with PVA glue. I already have much of the equipment from other projects (guillotine cutter, clamps, etc) so I figure I'd give it a try. My estimated cost would be in the few dollar range until I glue my hand to the wall and need to pay for drywall repairs.<br /> <br /> I'm looking at spiral binding some of the larger ones where I'd like them to lay flat but am disappointed that there's no good way to label the spines. I've also looked into velobinding and the machines are touch too expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T14:54:31-07:00","id":1258595,"title":"","content":"Sure, for the shorter books if you have the equipment already and want to do a perfect binding yourself, it shouldn't be too bad. For non-RPG projects, I've done a metal loop binding on bigger books (letting you get them flat) and put them in a binder cover to give them a spine to label... it's not pretty but it worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T23:16:45-07:00","id":1258832,"title":"","content":"If might not be too expensive to look at professional binding, many printing places can do it, but also check with colleges/universities. Thesis and the like need to be bound for submission","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T16:08:09-07:00","id":1259143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1258573-binding-your-own-paperbacks-and-hardbacks?p=1258832#post1258832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If might not be too expensive to look at professional binding, many printing places can do it, but also check with colleges/universities. Thesis and the like need to be bound for submission</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked into thesis binders as an options and many appeared to be mostly decorative so the costs were coming in at higher than say Staples. I've opted to try softcover as a first go with a few books under 120 sheets. If it's gorgeous or a dumpster fire, I'll share results either way. And in the mean time, will keep an eye out for a velobind machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}